; 17-grade-student-proofs-with-strict-mode.kurt
;
; Grade student proofs with strict mode
;
; Strict mode rejects `use`, `todo`, and the declarations that claim something about an operator
; (`flat`, `sym`, `builtin`) outside trusted theories; a `chain` there needs its rules proved
; before it. It also requires every
; symbol to be declared before its first use (`const`, `var`, `prop`, `infix`, ...: any declaration
; counts).

;     kurt --strict student-proof.kurt

; To provide instructor-approved axioms, put theory files in a separate directory and mark that
; directory trusted with `-p`:

;     kurt --strict -p course-theories student-proof.kurt

; The student file must prove its claims from Kurt's packaged theories and the theories in
; `course-theories`. Do not put solution facts in a theory students can edit.
;
; For exercises under development, `todo` is useful outside strict mode. For submitted work,
; strict mode ensures that a remaining `todo` or ad hoc axiom is an error rather than partial
; success.
